   "text": "I read the drawing as a macrocyclic peptide and wrote the SMILES by following the ring around.\n\n**Macrocycle, in order**\n1. L-2,4-diaminobutyric acid (Dab): the side-chain NH2 is on a CH2CH2 chain, and the \u03b1-NH is bonded to a CH2 on the pyridine.\n2. L-lysine, with a free (CH2)4NH2 side chain, joined to Dab through an amide.\n3. N-methyl-L-tryptophan, where the indole carries a 2-methyl group, joined to Lys through an N-methyl amide.\n4. A trisubstituted benzene ring, joined to the Trp C=O through an amide NH\u2013CH2.\n\n**Aryl and pyridine pieces**\n- The central benzene has the CH2NH at C1, a thioether S at C2 and Cl at C3. Positions C4 and C5 are CH, and C6 carries a 4-carboxyphenyl group.\n- The S links to C2 of a pyridine. The pyridine C3 carries the CH2 that goes to the Dab \u03b1-NH.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\nAll three wedged \u03b1-carbons work out as S, matching the L-amino acids. The Dab centre was assigned directly from the wedge. The Lys and Trp centres were assumed or checked against L-alanine, and I adjusted the @/@@ marks for the ring-closure and neighbour order in the SMILES.\n\nSMILES: NCC[C@@H]1NCc2cccnc2Sc2c(Cl)ccc(-c3ccc(C(=O)O)cc3)c2CNC(=O)[C@H](Cc2c(C)[nH]c3ccccc23)N(C)C(=O)[C@H](CCCCN)NC1=O"
